{
 "_comment": "Vegetation and rock catalogue for the grounds. scatter.py splits each scatter kind's points among its variants (weights) and writes one instance file per variant; the client build (tools/terrain/build_grounds.gd) cooks each variant's game model (tools/terrain/cook_vegetation.gd) and registers it with the Terrain3D instancer. `scale` multiplies the scatter scale (the source scans are life-size; the broadleaf scans are young trees). `collider` makes trunks/boulders solid for players and mobs (server and client build the same colliders from the same files). LOD distances are metres: [LOD0 end, LOD1 end, visibility end]; with two LODs the model disappears at LOD1 end. `simplify` (optional) rebuilds the LOD chain from the source LOD0 at those triangle fractions (cook_vegetation.gd). The quality preset scales every distance at runtime.",
